==Enemy==
The first boss of Uncanny Legends, Relic Bun-Bun has a 100% to curse your units, disabling their trait-targeting [[Special Abilities|abilities]] ([[Massive Damage|massive damage]], [[Weaken|weaken]], etc.) for a short period of time, though all other abilities are unaffected ([[Wave Attack]]s, [[Critical Hit]]s, etc.). Unlike most other variants of [[Teacher Bun Bun]], it isn't [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], making it that much more difficult to counter.

Other than what is stated above, this enemy is very similar to [[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|Mecha-Bun]]. It is different in that it deals half as much damage, gets knocked back half as many times, has longer [[Omni Strike]] reach, and moves slower.

==Strategy==
With huge DPS, an Omni Strike that increases its effective range, a 10-second Curse and 3,000,000 HP, this enemy is extremely dangerous. Its sheer DPS warrants the use of specialist meatshields like [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]] to stall, optionally aided by Research [[Cat Combo|Combos]]. For attackers, use [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relics]] that can outrange it, preferrably with other useful abilities, like [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Awakened Musashi]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]], [[Medusa Cat (Rare Cat)|Twintail Medusa Cat]], and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]. In its later appearances where it is backed by a multitude of nasty enemies, the assistance of [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] and Uril are absolutely necessary to cripple its advance.

