==Trivia==
*Relic Bun-Bun's description is accurate to its debut. It is stated to be a guardian of the realm of the [[:Category:Relic Enemies|ancients]], and it appears in the first [[Uncanny Legends]] stage, [[An Ancient Curse]]. The description also references cats that are [[Immune to Curse]], specifically the [[Stories of Legend]] [[Mythic Cat]]s that gain [[True Form]]s after beating [[Eldritch Forces]].
*Relic Bun-Bun, the first boss of Uncanny Legends, has several similarities to [[Zero Luza]], the final boss of Uncanny Legends. Both are ancient guardians that have Omni Strike and attack with their fists, both are variants of the bosses preceding them (Relic Bun-Bun is a variant of [[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|Mecha-Bun]], Zero Luza is a variant of [[Great Ape Luza]]), and both attack "mercilessly" (though their Japanese descriptions use different words for "merciless": 容赦なく ''yōshanaku'' and 無慈悲 ''mujihi'', respectively).
*Relic Bun-Bun and [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]] are the only variants of [[Teacher Bun Bun]] that don't have the [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait.

